Hi Cory

Thank you for your email.

I will do my best to respond to your queries; however, please note that our=
 review of the overpayment is not yet complete. In addition, there will be =
an overall review of your claim by my manager to determine the most appropr=
iate next steps.

Claim Status
Your last Income Protection payment was made on 28 May 2026, covering the p=
eriod 25 May 2026 to 31 May 2026.
Your benefit payments were temporarily suspended from 31 May 2026 while we =
investigate a potential overpayment for the period 7 April 2025 to 31 May 2=
026. Following our review of the payslips recently provided by Queensland H=
ealth, it appears that you initially returned to work on 7 April 2025. Howe=
ver, you continued to receive full Income Protection benefits throughout th=
is period.
As your employment income was not previously known to us, it had not been r=
ecorded within our system and therefore had not been taken into account whe=
n calculating your benefits. This has resulted in a potential overpayment. =
We are currently in the final stages of calculating the overpayment amount =
and are awaiting advice regarding the appropriate recovery process.
Please note that your payments have been suspended on a temporary basis onl=
y.
Once our review is complete, you may be entitled to ongoing benefits. Howev=
er, any future payments may need to be adjusted as part of the overpayment =
recovery process.
We acknowledge that on 16 March 2026 you contacted ART Life by email advisi=
ng that you had returned to work and requested that benefit payments cease.=
 However, we have no record of receiving notification from you in April or =
May 2025 advising that you had resumed work at that time. If you believe yo=
u previously notified us, please provide further details or forward any rel=
evant correspondence for our review.
Recalculation / overpayment

To calculate your Return to Employment Income, we reviewed your payslips co=
vering the period 7 April 2025 to 14 June 2026 and entered the gross earnin=
gs into our system.
The relevant Return to Employment Income definition and Partial Monthly Ben=
efit calculation formula are included below. For your reference, I have als=
o attached a copy of your QInsure Policy


[cid:image001.png@01DD2428.B11EF230]


[cid:image002.png@01DD2428.B11EF230]

I understand you have requested a complete schedule of Income Protection be=
nefits paid to date. I have asked our administration team to prepare this i=
nformation and will provide it to you once available.

Your Return to Employment Income for the period 7 April 2025 to 14 June 202=
6 has been calculated using the payslips provided directly by your employer=
.

At this stage, we believe the overpayment period is 7 April 2025 to 31 May =
2026, however the final overpayment amount has not yet been confirmed. We w=
ill contact you once this assessment has been completed.

As noted above, we acknowledge your email to ART Life dated 16 March 2026 r=
equesting that benefit payments cease. This information will be taken into =
consideration when determining the overpayment outcome.

The usual approach to recovering an overpayment is to reach an agreement wi=
th the member to reduce future Income Protection benefits by an agreed amou=
nt until the overpayment has been repaid. Once the overpayment has been fin=
alised, I will discuss the available options with you.

We understand that your last day worked was 13 June 2026. Based on informat=
ion recently received from your employer, they are currently unable to acco=
mmodate a graduated return to work due to the restrictions identified in yo=
ur Work Capabilities Checklist.

Given the length of this process, we have contacted your employer and advis=
ed that you may wish to access your available paid leave in the interim.

Medical disclosure / contact with your employer

We do not provide medical information to your employer or any other third p=
arty unless we have first obtained your authority to do so.

Our contact with your employer is limited to obtaining information relevant=
 to your employment, including payslips, leave history, return to work plan=
s, and related employment records.

Should you have any questions then please do not hesitate to contact me.

Kind Regards

James Zappia
Claims Manager
ART Life Insurance

Level 16
225 George Street
SYDNEY NSW 2000
Direct 07 3156 6730
P 1300 360 750 | F 07 3239 1139

