Dear Mr Zappia,

I refer to my income protection claim CLM-317073 (Party 195438787), employe=
r reference MSH-INJ-5795, and to QSuper Resolutions' letter of 28 May 2026 =
(complaint cf15866300-446968946), which confirmed you as Claims Manager and=
 that benefit payments were placed on hold effective 1 June 2026 pending re=
assessment.

I write to set out the confirmations and calculation rules I need so the re=
assessment is accurate, and so my employer's industrial handling of "IP" le=
ave is not based on a wrong characterisation of my claim and that my paysli=
ps have continued to contribute into the fund.

1. Claim status - please confirm in writing
(a) the date of the last IP benefit payment made to me;
(b) whether payments are ceased, on hold, or otherwise held only for recupe=
ration of overpayment (and from which date);
(c) whether any ongoing IP benefit is currently payable; and
(d) whether the file remains open only for reassessment / any overpayment a=
dministration (or, if not, what else remains open).

The above will assist me in the RTW integration which is now supported by m=
y treating Doctor.

I previously advised ART (March 2026)  and (May 2025) that I had returned t=
o work at reduced capacity and asked that benefits stop and that I had been=
 working against advice provided in February 2025 due to issue of MSH dismi=
ssing my employment entirely in October 2024. I need a clear written status=
 for my records and for employer correspondence.

2. Recalculation / overpayment - methodology required
I understand ART is obtaining payroll information from my employer. Please =
ensure the calculation:

A. Capacity
Over the return-to-work year period I have worked 0.56 of my full-time role=
 (56% FTE). Any partial temporary disablement / graduated RTW calculation m=
ust reflect actual work fraction and ordinary wages for hours worked, not f=
ull-time earnings, sick leave, annual leave or rostered days off unless per=
iod payslips show a different fraction for a defined sub-period (please the=
n use a period breakdown). All leave dates annual leave and sick leave was =
used in substance to manage my work load.

B. Exclude unfair dismissal settlement partial back payment settlement whic=
h included payment to my legal representatives.
Any partial back payment paid under my unfair dismissal / reinstatement set=
tlement deed is industrial settlement consideration, not "income earned whi=
le performing work for the purposes of IP offset." That amount must be carv=
ed out entirely from any "earnings while on benefits" figure. Including it =
would inflate earnings and overstate any overpayment. Please confirm in the=
 written breakdown that settlement / deed back-pay has been identified and =
excluded.

C. Include only
Ordinary wages for duties actually performed during periods when IP benefit=
s were still being paid (subject to the policy's partial payment formula).

D. Please provide in writing
(1) a complete payment schedule (date, gross amount, TTD/PTD basis, period =
covered);
(2) the earnings figures used and their source;
(3) the policy provisions applied for partial payment and recoupment;
(4) the period of reassessment;
(5) the resulting overpayment figure (if any) and;
(6) options for resolution if an overpayment is asserted which I believe it=
 has occured.

I will cooperate with reasonable requests. Please first use contribution / =
employer / account information already available to ART and only request fu=
rther payslips where necessary after that review - and only for periods of =
actual work, clearly separated from settlement payments. I have since downl=
oaded all payslips to confirm the figure of 0.56% workload per fortnight an=
d can be produced on request.

3. Medical disclosure (complaint cf15866300-446968946)
Beck's letter states ART Life's review found no indication that medical inf=
ormation from my claim file was disclosed by ART Life to external parties, =
and invites further information if my understanding differs. I have forward=
ed the report supplied to Louise which I was unaware of and is about me.

I maintain my concerns about the handling and circulation of highly sensiti=
ve medical material that originated in the claim context. I will provide fu=
rther particulars separately (and may copy Resolutions / AFCA as appropriat=
e).

Until written safeguards are clear, please:
* do not request further psychiatric / sensitive medical material beyond wh=
at is strictly necessary for benefit recalculation;
* confirm in writing what medical or capacity information has been (or will=
 be) requested from Metro South Health, and for what purpose; and
* confirm that claim medicals will not be disclosed to third parties involv=
ed in my legal proceedings without my prior written consent unless ART cont=
ends a specific legal obligation applies (please identify it).

4. Contact with my employer
Beck's letter notes you have contacted my employer for payroll information.=
 Please confirm what has been requested and received from Metro South Healt=
h / Injury Management (including around 13 July 2026), and whether any medi=
cal information (as opposed to payroll) was sought.

Workplace roster, ordinary pay, and suitable duties while I am certified fi=
t with restrictions are industrial matters with my employer. I ask that ART=
's characterisation of my claim status remain accurate and limited to insur=
ance administration.

5. Timeframe
Please provide written responses to section 1 and confirmation of the calcu=
lation rules in section 2A-2B within 10 business days, and the full recalcu=
lation package (section 2D) as soon as the payroll review is complete (and =
in any event within a stated timeframe).

Best contact: 0417 400 227 * coryshepherd1@hotmail.com

Yours sincerely,
Cory Lea Shepherd
